// `expected_generation` and writes the outbox event.
//
//   - Each `path` is first looked up in the base snapshot (the current
//     head of `branch_id`) as described under "Looking up a path".
//   - A change with `hash` replaces the file found, which keeps its
//     stored path; if no file is found, it adds a file at `path`, and the
//     names this creates (the segments of `path` that do not exist in the
//     base snapshot) must satisfy the write-time rules (see "File paths").
//     The content must have been uploaded to this workspace. `mode` is
//     optional: an explicit `mode` (420 regular, 493 executable) always
//     wins; without it, a replaced file keeps its existing mode, and a
//     new file gets 420.
//   - A change with `delete: true` removes the file found; the
//     write-time rules are not applied to it.
//   - Each path may appear once per request; the request needs at least
//     one change. The server limits the number of changes per commit
//     (`invalid_request` with `details.reason` = `too_many_changes` and
//     `details.max_changes`).
//   - The names a change creates are also checked against the names the
//     base snapshot has in that directory, including names another
//     change of the same request deletes: changing only the case of a
//     name, or turning a file into a directory, takes two commits.
//   - Changes that leave the tree as it is are refused
//     (`invalid_request` with `details.reason` = `no_changes`).
